    <tags>luz flux f.lux night-light blue-light color-temperature screen tray utility</tags>
    <summary>Warm your screen at night, from the tray, like f.lux</summary>
    <description><![CDATA[
A sun in the notification area that turns your screen's colour warmer after
sunset and back to daylight in the morning, like f.lux.

* Sunrise and sunset for where you are, guessed from your time zone: no
  location prompt, nothing over the network.
* Daytime, sunset and bedtime colours, down to 1200 K, with slow or fast fades.
* Bedtime mode: warmer still before you sleep, held until you wake.
* Pause for an hour or until sunrise, or nudge it warmer, cooler or dimmer.
* f.lux's keyboard shortcuts: Alt+End, Alt+PgUp/PgDn, Alt+Shift+PgUp/PgDn.
* Lifts Windows' limit on how warm the screen may go, as f.lux does.

One small executable, nothing else to install.
]]></description>
    <releaseNotes>https://github.com/kidchenko/luz/releases</releaseNotes>
  </metadata>
  <files>
    <file src="tools\**" target="tools" />
  </files>
</package>
